<ansi fg="black-bold">.:</ansi> <ansi fg="magenta">Help for </ansi><ansi fg="command">setcondition</ansi> <ansi fg="red">[Admin]</ansi>

The <ansi fg="command">setcondition</ansi> command applies a condition (a buff, a debuff, or
a status effect such as bleeding or stoneskin) to yourself or to a player or
mob in the room, by its id.

<ansi fg="yellow">Usage:</ansi>

  <ansi fg="command">setcondition [conditionId]</ansi>
  Apply a condition to yourself.

  <ansi fg="command">setcondition [name] [conditionId]</ansi>
  Apply a condition to a player or mob in the room.

  <ansi fg="command">setcondition search [text]</ansi>
  Search conditions by name.

  <ansi fg="command">setcondition list</ansi>
  List every condition and its id.

A condition whose spec stacks (multiple applications building up over time,
such as bleeding) cannot be applied this way; it can only be granted by
whatever move or effect actually produces it.

<ansi fg="black-bold">.:</ansi> <ansi fg="magenta">"buff" still works as an alias for this command.</ansi>
